<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fabre Geffrard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1806">1806</a>–<a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Fabre Nicolas Geffrard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fabre Geffrard was a Haitian general who overthrew Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque">Faustin I</a> in December 1858 and served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> from 1859 to 1867. He restored the republic, signed a concordat with the Vatican in 1860 and encouraged schools and African American immigration. Revolts forced him into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> in 1867.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fabre-geffrard.jpg" alt="Fabre Geffrard" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Studio of Eugène Disdéri · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fabre_Geffrard,_pr%C3%A9sident_d%27Ha%C3%AFti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
